+## Using multiple files
+
+By default tally reads and writes `tally.json` in the current directory. Pass
+`--store` to use a different file:
+
+```
+tally --store work.json add 45 transport
+tally --store personal.json report --month 2024-03
+```
+
+This is the simplest way to keep separate expense logs (work vs. personal,
+different years, etc.).
+
+## Running the tests
+
+```
+python -m pytest
+```
+
+The suite must pass with zero failures and zero warnings. Tests that pin specific
+currency-conversion totals are there intentionally — if you change a rate in
+`tally/rates.py`, update those tests in the same commit.
+
